From: Devin Phat <devin.phat97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:05:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: remove resource from state when Railway reports not
 found

Terraform expects Read to call resp.State.RemoveResource when the remote
object no longer exists. Returning an error instead breaks refresh after
out-of-band deletion and tooling built on the provider (Crossplane/Upjet).
Adds isNotFoundError (GraphQL response errors containing "not found") and
applies it to railway_project; other resources to follow.
